s_01KEZF7C006X9JK6NZNA2SM9XD". object.delivery_mode (Optional): string. How issue delivered the invoice. Value enum: "email", "caller_managed". object.due_date (Optional): string. Calendar due date in YYYY-MM-DD format, interpreted in timezone (UTC when absent). The outstanding balance becomes overdue only after this date ends. Automatic collection runs at the later of issue and the start of this date. With payment terms, issue computes this date from issued_at. Absent when there is no due date. Format: date. Example: "2026-08-02". object.external_reference_id (Required): string or null. Caller-owned identifier for this resource in an external system. Use it as your sync key: it isn't printed on the invoice. `null` when unset. minLength: 1. maxLength: 255. Example: "warehouse-1842". object.footer (Required): string or null. Fine print at the bottom of the invoice and PDF. It cannot change after issue. `null` when unset. object.invoice_id (Required): string. Flint invoice ID. Example: "inv_01KEZF7C00A5GEBMWHEAJFSAR4". object.invoice_number (Optional): string. Sequential document number assigned when the invoice is issued. Numbering is per merchant, with test and live mode numbered independently. object.is_overdue (Required): boolean. Whether the invoice is open or partially_paid and past due with a balance remaining. Without schedule_entries, the due_date has ended in timezone (UTC when absent) and outstanding_money is above zero; with them, at least one entry is overdue. Computed when the invoice is read. object.issued_at (Optional): string. When the invoice was issued. Absent on a draft. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.late_fees (Required): Array of {@see InvoiceLateFeeInput}. Late fees assessed on this invoice, each with its paid, waived, written-off, and outstanding amounts. settlement_amounts.late_fee_money is their assessed total minus waivers. object.late_fees[] (Value): {@see InvoiceLateFeeInput}. A charge assessed because an invoice payment is overdue. object.memo (Required): string or null. Message to the customer, printed on the invoice and PDF. It cannot change after issue. `null` when unset. object.merchant_id (Required): string. Merchant that owns this invoice. Example: "mer_01KEZF7C00KPYH1DDFPCCX3B6E". object.metadata (Optional): {@see MetadataMapInput}. Caller-owned metadata. Caller-owned key-value data stored on a resource. Keys starting with flint_ are reserved for Flint and are not returned. Writes follow the limits on MetadataInput and MetadataPatchInput; maps written before those limits may not satisfy them. object.order (Optional): {@see ExpandedOrderSummaryInput} or null. Summary of the backing order. Returned only with expand=order. Present only when `expand` includes `order`; `null` when expanded and there is no related order. object.order.anyOf[1] (Value): {@see ExpandedOrderSummaryInput}. An order's summary fields, including status, payment and refund status, and pricing and settlement amounts, returned when the order is expanded. object.order.anyOf[2] (Value): null. object.order_id (Required): string. The order this invoice bills. Every invoice has one; quick pay creates it. Example: "ord_01KEZF7C0054GQKJ142A8X367A". object.paid_at (Optional): string. When the invoice most recently became paid. Cleared when status leaves paid and set again on a later paid transition. Format: date-time. Example: "2026-08-02T16:00:00Z". object.payment_due (Required): {@see InvoicePaymentDueInput}. The resolved due-date policy. Send this object back when updating the draft; payment_terms captures the term's current revision again. The invoice due-date policy resolved at write time. The object can be sent back when updating a draft. object.payment_terms_snapshot (Optional): {@see InvoicePaymentTermsSnapshotInput}. The payment term captured on the draft, with its due date rule and late fee policy. Later changes to the payment term don't affect this invoice. The payment terms saved on an invoice: